<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof for Monotonic Lower Bound of Attention Entropy</h2>

<div id="A1.Thmdefi1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmdefi1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmdefi1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lower Bound of Attention Entropy)<span id="A1.Thmdefi1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmdefi1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmdefi1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmdefi1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmdefi1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,\cdot}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝛂</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,\cdot}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be the attention distribution of node <math id="A1.Thmdefi1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A1.Thmdefi1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> nodes. Suppose each entry satisfies <math id="A1.Thmdefi1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,j}\geq\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝛂</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,j}\geq\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the attention entropy <math id="A1.Thmdefi1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}(v_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(v_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> admits the following strict lower bound:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}(v_{i})\geq-\left[1-(n-1)\epsilon\right]\log\left[1-(n-1)\epsilon\right]-(n-1)\epsilon\log\epsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(v_{i})\geq-\left[1-(n-1)\epsilon\right]\log\left[1-(n-1)\epsilon\right]-(n-1)\epsilon\log\epsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is a lower bound for all elements of <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,\cdot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,\cdot}</annotation></semantics></math>. The minimum entropy under this constraint is attained when one entry takes the maximum possible weight and the remaining <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n-1)</annotation></semantics></math> entries equal <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, </span><span id="A1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span><span id="A1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text">,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\boldsymbol{\alpha}}_{i,\cdot}=\left(1-(n-1)\epsilon,\epsilon,\dots,\epsilon\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜶</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\boldsymbol{\alpha}}_{i,\cdot}=\left(1-(n-1)\epsilon,\epsilon,\dots,\epsilon\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">The attention entropy of this distribution is</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{\min}(v_{i})=-\left[1-(n-1)\epsilon\right]\log\left[1-(n-1)\epsilon\right]-(n-1)\epsilon\log\epsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{\min}(v_{i})=-\left[1-(n-1)\epsilon\right]\log\left[1-(n-1)\epsilon\right]-(n-1)\epsilon\log\epsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since the Shannon entropy is strictly concave, any deviation from this distribution increases the entropy. Therefore, for any valid distribution <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,\cdot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,\cdot}</annotation></semantics></math> with elements bounded below by <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}(v_{i})\geq\mathcal{H}_{\min}(v_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(v_{i})\geq\mathcal{H}_{\min}(v_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We now provide the proof for Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmdefi1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Monotonic Lower Bond of Attention Entropy). ‣ 3.1 Attention Entropy ‣ 3 Over-Aggregating in Graph Transformers ‣ Relieving the Over-Aggregating Effect in Graph Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> based on Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmdefi1" title="Lemma A.1 (Lower Bound of Attention Entropy). ‣ Appendix A Proof for Monotonic Lower Bound of Attention Entropy ‣ Relieving the Over-Aggregating Effect in Graph Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmdefi1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Monotonic Lower Bond of Attention Entropy). ‣ 3.1 Attention Entropy ‣ 3 Over-Aggregating in Graph Transformers ‣ Relieving the Over-Aggregating Effect in Graph Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a></span> (Monotonic Lower Bound of Attention Entropy). <span id="A1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,\cdot}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝛂</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,\cdot}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be the attention distribution of node <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> nodes. The attention entropy <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}(v_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(v_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> admits a lower bound that increases monotonically with <math id="A1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">To show that <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{\min}(v_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{\min}(v_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> increases monotonically with <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, we compute its derivative with respect to <math id="A1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex5X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d\mathcal{H}_{\min}(v_{i})}{dn}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d\mathcal{H}_{\min}(v_{i})}{dn}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\epsilon\log\left[1-(n-1)\epsilon\right]+\left[1-(n-1)\epsilon\right]\frac{\epsilon}{\left[1-(n-1)\epsilon\right]}-\epsilon\log\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\epsilon\log\left[1-(n-1)\epsilon\right]+\left[1-(n-1)\epsilon\right]\frac{\epsilon}{\left[1-(n-1)\epsilon\right]}-\epsilon\log\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex5Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\epsilon\log\left[1-(n-1)\epsilon\right]+\epsilon-\epsilon\log\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\epsilon\log\left[1-(n-1)\epsilon\right]+\epsilon-\epsilon\log\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex5Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\epsilon\log\frac{1-(n-1)\epsilon}{\epsilon}+\epsilon." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\epsilon\log\frac{1-(n-1)\epsilon}{\epsilon}+\epsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\boldsymbol{\alpha}}_{i,\cdot}=(1-(n-1)\epsilon,\epsilon,\cdots,\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜶</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\boldsymbol{\alpha}}_{i,\cdot}=(1-(n-1)\epsilon,\epsilon,\cdots,\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> denoting the most non-uniform distribution <math id="A1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,\cdot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,\cdot}</annotation></semantics></math> requires <math id="A1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\epsilon\leq 1/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\epsilon\leq 1/n</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that <math id="A1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-(n-1)\epsilon\geq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-(n-1)\epsilon\geq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d\mathcal{H}_{\min}(v_{i})}{dn}&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d\mathcal{H}_{\min}(v_{i})}{dn}&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">This confirms that <math id="A1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{\min}(v_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{\min}(v_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> increases monotonically with <math id="A1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Detailed Derivation</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide a detailed derivation for Eq. <a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.2 Over-Aggregating ‣ 3 Over-Aggregating in Graph Transformers ‣ Relieving the Over-Aggregating Effect in Graph Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. Let <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{\mathbf{R}}=\mathrm{\mathbf{QK}}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐑</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐐𝐊</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{\mathbf{R}}=\mathrm{\mathbf{QK}}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>. Given the attention scores formulated in Eq. <a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3.1 Attention Entropy ‣ 3 Over-Aggregating in Graph Transformers ‣ Relieving the Over-Aggregating Effect in Graph Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, the gradient of <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{\mathbf{W}}_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{\mathbf{W}}_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> can be derived as</p>
<table id="A2.Ex7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex7X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,j}}{\partial\mathrm{\mathbf{W}}_{Q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,j}}{\partial\mathrm{\mathbf{W}}_{Q}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{n}\frac{\partial\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,j}}{\partial\mathrm{\mathbf{R}}_{i,k}}\frac{\partial\mathrm{\mathbf{R}}_{i,k}}{\mathrm{\mathbf{W}}_{Q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{n}\frac{\partial\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,j}}{\partial\mathrm{\mathbf{R}}_{i,k}}\frac{\partial\mathrm{\mathbf{R}}_{i,k}}{\mathrm{\mathbf{W}}_{Q}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex7Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{n}\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,j}\left(\delta_{j,k}-\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,k}\right)\frac{\partial}{\partial\mathrm{\mathbf{W}}_{Q}}\mathrm{\mathbf{X}}_{i,\cdot}\mathrm{\mathbf{W}}_{Q}\mathrm{\mathbf{W}}_{K}^{\top}\mathrm{\mathbf{X}}_{k,\cdot}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{n}\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,j}\left(\delta_{j,k}-\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,k}\right)\frac{\partial}{\partial\mathrm{\mathbf{W}}_{Q}}\mathrm{\mathbf{X}}_{i,\cdot}\mathrm{\mathbf{W}}_{Q}\mathrm{\mathbf{W}}_{K}^{\top}\mathrm{\mathbf{X}}_{k,\cdot}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex7Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{n}\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,j}\left(\delta_{j,k}-\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,k}\right)\mathrm{\mathbf{X}}_{i,\cdot}^{\top}\mathrm{\mathbf{X}}_{k,\cdot}\mathrm{\mathbf{W}}_{K}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{n}\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,j}\left(\delta_{j,k}-\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,k}\right)\mathrm{\mathbf{X}}_{i,\cdot}^{\top}\mathrm{\mathbf{X}}_{k,\cdot}\mathrm{\mathbf{W}}_{K}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex7Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,j}\!\left(\mathrm{\mathbf{X}}_{i,\cdot}^{\top}\mathrm{\mathbf{X}}_{j,\cdot}\mathrm{\mathbf{W}}_{K}^{\top}-\!\sum_{\tiny k=1}^{n}\!\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,k}\mathrm{\mathbf{X}}_{i,\cdot}^{\top}\mathrm{\mathbf{X}}_{k,\cdot}\mathrm{\mathbf{W}}_{K}^{\top}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,j}\!\left(\mathrm{\mathbf{X}}_{i,\cdot}^{\top}\mathrm{\mathbf{X}}_{j,\cdot}\mathrm{\mathbf{W}}_{K}^{\top}-\!\sum_{\tiny k=1}^{n}\!\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,k}\mathrm{\mathbf{X}}_{i,\cdot}^{\top}\mathrm{\mathbf{X}}_{k,\cdot}\mathrm{\mathbf{W}}_{K}^{\top}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{j,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{j,k}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sign function. When <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=j</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{j,k}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{j,k}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, otherwise <math id="A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{j,k}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{j,k}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
